#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/go-oauth-cli-tutorial/en.mdx:245
#: src/guides/oauth-cli-tutorial/en.mdx:197
#, no-wrap
msgid "A few things to keep in mind:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/go-oauth-cli-tutorial/en.mdx:249
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"- **This is for local development.** The localhost client won't work in production. For a production-ready Go example with SQLite persistence and multiple commands, see the [go-oauth-cli-app](https://github.com/bluesky-social/cookbook/tree/main/go-oauth-cli-app) in the Cookbook.\n"
"- **Sessions are in-memory.** Every run requires re-authorization. The Cookbook example shows how to persist sessions with SQLite.\n"
"- **Scopes.** This tutorial requests only the base `atproto` scope. To read or write data on behalf of the user, you'll need additional [scopes](/guides/scopes).\n"
msgstr ""

